{"reason": "The current baseline suffers from premature early stopping at tree 168 because decision trees partition feature space into constant step functions and cannot extrapolate continuous monotonic price appreciation into out-of-time test periods. Modifying data_processing_and_feature_engineering, model_design, and training_evaluation addresses this root cause by decomposing the prediction task into a parametric extrapolatable hierarchical trend plus stationary tree-modeled residuals, activating native categorical splitting, and applying recency sample weighting to align gradients with modern market dynamics.", "module": ["data_processing_and_feature_engineering", "model_design", "training_evaluation"], "plan": {"data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "WHAT: Fit a regularized hierarchical linear time-trend estimator across national and county/district levels on pre-validation history to generate a stationary residual target y_residual = target - y_trend, while preparing categorical features and computing temporal recency deltas. WHY: Tree-based gradient boosters cannot extrapolate continuous price appreciation into future unseen timeframes, which caused target saturation; detrending leaves a stationary structural target representing relative property premiums. HOW: Fit empirical Bayes smoothed linear trend slopes per county and district shrunk toward the national slope on pre-2016-07 data, compute y_trend for all splits, compute y_train_residual for training, convert high-cardinality location and property columns to category types, and compute days-to-cutoff for sample weighting. INTERFACE: Retain existing temporal out-of-time split masks, X_train, X_val, X_test, val_true_price, test_ids, and all engineered spatial features.", "model_design": "WHAT: Design a two-stage additive model architecture where parametric hierarchical linear trend projections are combined additively with a LightGBM regressor trained on stationary residuals with native categorical handling. WHY: Additive decomposition allows the linear model to handle forward extrapolation across time boundaries while enabling LightGBM to focus its capacity on complex non-linear spatial and structural property interactions without time-induced split distortion. HOW: Configure LightGBM with categorical_feature list covering district, county, property_type, tenure, is_new_build, and sale_category with cat_smooth=20.0 and min_data_per_group=20, and define the additive reconstruction function y_hat = y_hat_trend + y_hat_residual. INTERFACE: Preserve model_params dictionary structure, random_state=SEED, n_jobs=32, and the model persistence mechanism at ./working/lgbm_best_model.txt.", "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Implement exponential recency sample weighting in the LightGBM training loop, reconstruct additive predictions on validation and test partitions, and evaluate against the official log10 RMSE metric. WHY: Equal sample weighting forces trees to split equally on obsolete market conditions, whereas exponential recency weighting focuses gradient descent on contemporary price relationships that directly inform the 2017 out-of-time evaluation period. HOW: Supply sample_weight = np.exp(-0.0003 * days_to_val) to model.fit(), reconstruct final validation predictions via 10 ** (y_val_trend + y_val_residual_pred), calculate score using official_log10_rmse, and export clipped integer predictions to ./submission/submission.csv following sample submission specifications. INTERFACE: Retain official_log10_rmse, final_val_score reporting format, test submission schema (id, price), and all verification assertions."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
  "reason": "The current baseline suffers from premature early stopping at tree 168 because decision trees partition feature space into constant step functions and cannot extrapolate continuous monotonic price appreciation into out-of-time test periods. Modifying data_processing_and_feature_engineering, model_design, and training_evaluation addresses this root cause by decomposing the prediction task into a parametric extrapolatable hierarchical trend plus stationary tree-modeled residuals, activating native categorical splitting, and applying recency sample weighting to align gradients with modern market dynamics.",
