    "model_design": "WHAT: Design a two-stage additive model architecture where parametric hierarchical linear trend projections are combined additively with a LightGBM regressor trained on stationary residuals with native categorical handling. WHY: Additive decomposition allows the linear model to handle forward extrapolation across time boundaries while enabling LightGBM to focus its capacity on complex non-linear spatial and structural property interactions without time-induced split distortion. HOW: Configure LightGBM with categorical_feature list covering district, county, property_type, tenure, is_new_build, and sale_category with cat_smooth=20.0 and min_data_per_group=20, and define the additive reconstruction function y_hat = y_hat_trend + y_hat_residual. INTERFACE: Preserve model_params dictionary structure, random_state=SEED, n_jobs=32, and the model persistence mechanism at ./working/lgbm_best_model.txt.",
