numeric_features, cat_feature_names, train/val/test splits, and ensure all newly derived interaction and recency columns are concatenated into the dense feature tensors.", "model_design": "WHAT: Upgrade PropertyPriceNet's linear trend highway into a Spatially Conditioned Trend Highway by feeding explicit cross-interaction terms between normalized elapsed time and hierarchical spatial/type price anchors (such as time * te_county, time * te_district, time * te_property_type) directly into the linear highway, while increasing ResNet dropout from 0.20 to 0.30. WHY: UK property prices exhibit stark regional divergence (e.g., 8-10% annual inflation in London versus 2-3% in northern districts), making a single scalar time slope inadequate for out-of-time forward extrapolation into 2017. HOW: In PropertyPriceNet, construct explicit linear highway features by multiplying time_elapsed_years with key target encodings, update linear_highway to nn.Linear(num_linear_feats, 1, bias=False) covering both baseline levels and interaction slopes, and pass the increased dropout rate to TabularResidualBlock and projection layers. INTERFACE: Preserve get_model_and_optimizer function signature, model forward pass signature (x_dense, x_cat), Log10RMSELoss class, and AdamW / CosineAnnealingLR setup.", "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Incorporate exponential recency sample weighting into the Log10RMSELoss training objective (weight = exp(0.20 * time_elapsed_years)), raise AdamW weight decay to 1e-3, and evaluate the final predictions against the official log10 RMSE metric. WHY: Unweighted training forces the network to expend equal gradient capacity fitting outdated 2010 transaction patterns, whereas exponential recency weighting focuses optimization on modern market relationships that govern the 2016 validation and 2017 test periods. HOW: Modify Log10RMSELoss to accept optional sample weights computed from time_elapsed_years during training iterations, update the training loop to pass sample weights to the loss calculation, keep validation loss unweighted for strict official metric reporting, and export clipped price predictions (minimum 1.0) formatted with columns id and price to ./submission/submission.csv. INTERFACE: Retain exact batch size, training loop structure, best_model_path saving logic, verification assertions, and final validation score printout."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
