ion rates diverge sharply at the district level rather than broad counties, requiring localized linear extrapolation into the 2017 out-of-time horizon; MSE loss on log10(price) eliminates denominator gradient distortion and directly optimizes the squared log-error metric. HOW: In SemiParametricTabResNet, locate self.dist_cat_idx, create trend_bypass_dist_slope and trend_bypass_dist_intercept initialized to zeros, add their contributions in forward(), and replace input_proj with a GLU gated linear block; instantiate criterion = nn.MSELoss(). INTERFACE: Preserve SemiParametricTabResNet constructor parameters and forward(x_cat, x_num) signature, optimizer parameter grouping logic, and model output shapes.", "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Expand the training schedule by increasing max_epochs from 6 to 12, raise early stopping patience from 2 to 3, and adjust the Cosine Annealing learning rate schedule over the extended step count. WHY: The baseline run was still descending steeply at epoch 6 (from 0.2515 to 0.2501 to 0.2494) after only 5 minutes of execution, demonstrating that the model was undertrained on the 4M row dataset. HOW: Update max_epochs = 12 and patience = 3, recompute total_steps = max_epochs * len(train_loader) passed to build_optimizer_and_scheduler, maintain gradient clipping at max_norm=2.0, retain the 1-epoch post-validation fine-tuning step on the full dataset, and generate final test predictions. INTERFACE: Retain official log10-RMSE metric reporting ('Final Validation Score: {final_score}'), model checkpointing at ./working/best_model.pt, test ID alignment, and submission CSV structure at ./submission/submission.csv."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
